76-4 WE CONCUR: Lee, J.P.T.20'}, {'verified': 'true', 'case_name': 'State v. Waldon', 'canonical_name': 'State v. Waldon', 'citation': '202 P.3d 325', 'canonical_citation': '202 P.3d 325', 'url': 'https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2515709/state-v-waldon/', 'canonical_date': '2009-02-23', 'court': 'Court of Appeals of Washington', 'docket_number': '61019-8-I', 'source': 'CourtListener', 'confidence': 0.9, 'parallel_citations': [], 'verification_method': 'courtlistener_api', 'extracted_case_name': None, 'hinted_case_name': None, 'is_parallel_citation': True, 'primary_citation': '148 Wn. App. 952', 'is_complex_citation': True, 'context': 'IN THE SUPREME COURT OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON No. 102976-4 En BancFiled: June 12, 2025 v. Petitioners, JOHN DOE P, JOHN DOE Q, JOHN ) ) DOE R, and JOHN DOE S, as ) individuals and on behalf of others ) similarly situated, ) ) ) ) ) THURSTON COUNTY, a municipal ) ) organization, and its departments ) the THURSTON COUNTY ) PROSECUTING ATTORNEY and ) THURSTON COUNTY SHERIFF, ) ) ) ) ) ) Respondents/Cross ) ) Petitioners. _______________________________) DONNA ZINK and JEFF ZINK, a married couple, Respondents , YU, J. — This case involves a postdismissal challenge to a trial court’s order permanently sealing the petitioners’ actual names and allowing them to be FILE IN CLERK’S OFFICE SUPREME COURT, STATE OF WASHINGTON JUNE 12, 2025THIS OPINION WAS FILED FOR RECORD AT 8 A.M.ON JUNE 12, 2025SARAH R.PENDLETON SUPREME COURT CLERK John Doe P et al. v. Thurston County et al., No. 102976-4 identified by pseudonym in court records. The underlying case is a PRA1 injunction action, in which the petitioners (John Does P, Q, R, and S) sought to enjoin Thurston County (County) from releasing unredacted sex offender records in response to cross petitioner Donna Zink’s PRA request. Over the course of these proceedings, nearly all of the Does’ PRA exemption claims have been rejected on the merits, and Zink received most of the records she requested